* Corrected Multi-column PWL from file using XSPICE filesource

* 1. Define the File Models (One for each column output)
* Note: amploffset and amplscale must match the number of output columns 
* you are pulling (1 for each individual source here).
* .model fsrc_col1 filesource(file="waveforms.txt" amplstep=false timerelative=false
* +                           amploffset=[0] amplscale=[1.0])

* .model fsrc_col2 filesource(file="waveforms.txt" amplstep=false timerelative=false
* +                           amploffset=[0 0] amplscale=[0 1.0])

.model fsrc_col3 filesource(file="waveforms.txt" amplstep=false timerelative=false
+                           amploffset=[0 0 0] amplscale=[1.0 1.0 1.0])

* 2. Instantiate the Sources using 'A' devices
* %v[...] tells the simulator these are analog voltage outputs
* We pass all columns into the device, but the amplscale handles which one is active.
* Acol1 %v[node_v1] fsrc_col1
* Acol2 %v[0 node_v2] fsrc_col2
* Acol3 %v[0 0 node_v3] fsrc_col3

Acol1 %v[node_v1 0 0] fsrc_col3
Acol2 %v[0 node_v2 0] fsrc_col3
Acol3 %v[0 0 node_v3] fsrc_col3

* Dummy loads to keep the matrix happy
R1 node_v1 0 1k
R2 node_v2 0 1k
R3 node_v3 0 1k

* 3. Simulation Controls
.tran 0.1m 5m

.control
  run
  plot v(node_v1) v(node_v2) v(node_v3)
.endc

.end